"firstrun.tryIt.body" = "This is your dictation key. Press it, say something, press it again.";
"firstrun.tryIt.note" = "The text lands in the field below and nowhere else: while this window is open, I type only here.";
"firstrun.tryIt.title" = "Try it right now";
"firstrun.welcome.body" = "Press the key, say a sentence, press it again. The text appears where your cursor was: in an email, in a chat, in the terminal.";
"firstrun.welcome.note" = "It all runs right on your Mac. No audio, no text leaves it.";
"firstrun.welcome.title" = "You talk, I type";
"firstrun.whenItBreaks.body" = "Text didn't paste? It isn't lost. The badge expands and shows it, and you can copy it from there.";
"firstrun.whenItBreaks.note" = "Misheard a word? Just correct it right in the text. I notice the edit and ask whether to remember it: say yes, and from then on I write it your way. I never put anything into the dictionary on my own.\n\nKey taken by another app? Click it in the settings and set your own shortcut.\n\nThis window, the settings and the history all open from the icon in the menu bar.";
"firstrun.whenItBreaks.title" = "If something goes wrong";
"firstrun.whereItLives.body" = "Do not look for me in the Dock: my icon is at the top right, next to the clock. Click it and the menu opens.";
"firstrun.whereItLives.note" = "History, replacements, settings and meeting recording all open from that menu. It also shows what I am busy with right now.\n\nI start together with your Mac. Do not want that: turn it off in the settings.";
"firstrun.whereItLives.title" = "I live in the menu bar";
"firstrun.windowTitle" = "Meet iriz";
