"firstrun.plate.title" = "The plate is always on screen";
"firstrun.plate.body" = "A glass drop sits at the bottom of your screen. While you are silent it stays small and does nothing. Start talking and a wave runs through it: that is the answer to «can it hear me».";
"firstrun.plate.note" = "Point at it with the mouse and the drop opens into a row of buttons: record, prompt, translate, language, history, settings. Click it and a panel with the text opens.\n\nYou can drag the plate: it snaps to one of twelve spots along the edges of the screen. There are three ways out of the open panel: the cross, Escape, and a click past the buttons.";
"settings.napominaniyaNaPlashke" = "Reminders on the plate";
"settings.napominaniyaNapominayutKlavishu" = "The reminders name the key that ends the recording, and Escape for cancelling. Off by default: there is no point naming the key you are holding under your finger, and the words cover the wave — the thing the plate exists for. Turn them on for the first few days if that feels calmer.";
"settings.klikniPoSochetaniyuChtoby" = "Click the shortcut on the right and press a new one — it gets recorded. The shortcut works right after you press Save. To undo a switch, press the conversion shortcut once more.";
